        "original_id": "a9e1d299-54a6-56d8-a880-4fc2ea3001f7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Margarita Lozano, Luis Buñuel, Sergio Leone, Pier Paolo Pasolini, Paolo Taviani, Vittorio Taviani, Nanni Moretti, Claude Berri, Marcel Pagnol, Carmelo Gómez, Icíar Bollaín, Francisco Algora\n- Products: Viridiana, A Fistful of Dollars, Pigsty, The Night of the Shooting Stars, Kaos, Good Morning Babylon, La messa è finita, Jean de Florette, Manon of the Spring, Manon des Sources, Nos miran\n- Topics: film collaborations, film adaptation\n\nFacts:\n- Margarita Lozano worked with Luis Buñuel in \"Viridiana,\" Sergio Leone in \"A Fistful of Dollars,\" and Pier Paolo Pasolini in \"Pigsty.\"\n- Margarita Lozano worked with the Taviani brothers in \"The Night of the Shooting Stars,\" \"Kaos,\" and \"Good Morning Babylon,\" and with Nanni Moretti in \"La messa è finita.\"\n- Margarita Lozano appeared in Claude Berri's two-film project consisting of \"Jean de Florette\" and \"Manon of the Spring.\"\n- \"Manon des Sources,\" meaning \"Manon of the Spring,\" is a 1986 French-language film.\n- Claude Berri directed \"Manon des Sources\" as the second of two films adapted from Marcel Pagnol's 1966 two-volume novel.\n- Marcel Pagnol wrote the 1966 two-volume novel underlying \"Manon des Sources\" based on his own earlier film of the same title.\n- \"Nos miran\" is a thriller starring Carmelo Gómez with Icíar Bollaín, Margarita Lozano, and Francisco Algora.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
